<x-admin-layout title="User guide">
    <div class="admin-content">
        <div class="admin-page-heading"><div><p class="admin-eyebrow">Workspace help</p><h1>User guide</h1><p>A practical guide to the Father's Heart workspace. The menu and actions you can use depend on your assigned permissions.</p></div></div>
        <section class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>1. Sign in and navigate</h2><p>Sign in with your staff email and password. Use the expandable sidebar sections to find your work area. Select a section again to collapse it. Use My profile to update your account details or password; sign out when you finish.</p><p>If an area is missing or a page says access is denied, ask an administrator to review your role and its individual route permissions.</p></section>
        <section class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>2. Register a person</h2><p>Open People &amp; care → People and choose Register person. Enter the available details and save. If a phone number matches another record, review the warning before confirming: a shared number does not necessarily mean the person is a duplicate.</p><p>Use the name, number and date filters to find people. Exports are available where your role permits them. Historical records with an unknown original registration date are excluded from registration-date filters.</p></section>
        <section class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>3. Complete an assessment</h2><p>From the person record or people list, select Add assessment. Choose a distribution event and location where appropriate. You can use the step-by-step or full-form view and save the information available.</p><p>The intake code is generated by the configured settings. A device considered is not proof it was handed over. Historical device and recorded-date values are unverified; an old date may reflect a later edit.</p></section>
        <section class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>4. Photos and consent</h2><p>On a supported phone or computer, add a before or after photo by choosing a file or using the device camera when offered. Historical photo matches are private and unverified; a reused filename may belong to another person. Confirm identity before relying on a match.</p><p>A photo or historical reference does not grant permission to publish it. Record and verify the appropriate signed consent separately before publication.</p></section>
        <section class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>5. Distribution events</h2><p>Open Distributions → Distribution events to plan, view or update an event. Assign the event to an assessment to include that person in its event list. Historical events are preserved registry references; review their names, dates and districts before treating them as confirmed.</p></section>
        <section class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>6. Inventory and historical stock</h2><p>Open Inventory → Stock management to add an item. Record its opening balance only after a physical stock count has been reviewed and approved. After that, record stock received or issued with the date and an optional reference.</p><p>Historical stock contains old snapshots and counters, not verified current balances. Use the separate Historical stock page to filter or export references; these do not change current inventory.</p></section>
        <section class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>7. Staff, roles and permissions</h2><p>Under User management, authorized staff can create accounts and assign existing roles. Create the role first if it is not listed. Each role needs <strong>access-admin</strong> to enter the workspace plus the individual routes needed for the work.</p><p>Staff may use Request staff registration on the sign-in screen to submit their name, email, password and requested role. No login account is created until a super administrator opens User management &rarr; Registration requests, checks the person's identity and approves a final role. Rejected applicants may apply again. The system does not automatically notify applicants; contact them securely about the decision.</p><p>Volunteer accounts can be approved. Record-assignment restrictions are not yet available, so their role permissions can give access to all records in permitted areas. Review those permissions carefully.</p><p>Form pages and save actions are separate permissions: for example, give the GET route to open a form and the POST or PUT route to save it. Some actions remain restricted to super administrators or have additional record-level protections. Users with multiple roles receive their combined permissions.</p><p>Historical team entries do not automatically become login accounts. A super administrator can create a new account with a new password or explicitly link an existing account after confirming identity. Share passwords securely.</p></section>
        <section class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>8. Filters, exports and installation</h2><p>Use a table's filter to narrow its results. Read the export label: some downloads cover all matching records, while current-page exports cover only the visible page. CSV files can be opened in Excel. Access to specific export routes is controlled by permissions.</p><p>Where supported, use the Install app button or your browser's install option. Phone installation and access depend on a reachable address and browser security requirements; a computer's <strong>127.0.0.1</strong> address is not reachable from another phone.</p></section>
        <section class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>9. Children’s therapy</h2><p>Open Children’s therapy &rarr; Children, choose Register child and search the People registry by name or phone. If the child is not listed, register them in People first, then return to link the record. A guardian’s phone may be shared by siblings.</p><p>Complete the initial registration in steps or full view. Record each consent purpose separately and store supporting documents privately. From the child’s record, choose Record visit and select all services involved. Visit reports distinguish completed visits from missed or cancelled visits; CSV exports can be opened in Excel.</p><p>Therapy settings control the services and suggested registration options. Individual record assignments are not currently enforced; therapy permissions may grant access to all therapy records in the permitted area. Review staff roles carefully.</p></section>
    </div>
</x-admin-layout>
